From: laudney <106273+laudney@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:45:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(lanes): release a stream that finishes on its first token

Upstream TensorFold commit by laudney, ported onto this series (upstream main ed39acc5aac1).

On the default open path a stream that finishes on its first token
ran its trace before releasing its lane, so a failed trace left the
backend's caches held: the host discards only unfinished streams,
and nothing released them again. The release now runs deferred
around the trace, as the first-before-draft path already does, and
two tests cover an unresolvable trace and every trace allocation
failure on that path.

(cherry picked from commit ed39acc5aac1973cb1f438533703a27edee56084)
